course: dictionary
lesson: 4266
title: Words on the gravestone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gravestone is a stone put on a grave. It shows the name of the person buried there, and often words about them. You might read gravestones in a history lesson, in an old churchyard, or in a spooky story.
explain: Context helps you work out what a word means. «The words on the gravestone» tells you that a gravestone has writing on it. An «old gravestone» is one that has stood for a long time, so the writing may use old-fashioned words.
explain: Some gravestones use old sayings. «Departed this life» means died, so the stone may not say died outright. «A good innings» comes from cricket and means a long, full life. Ask yourself what the words are saying, not only what each word means.
fact: A gravestone is a stone put on a grave.
fact: A gravestone shows the name of the person buried there, and often words about them.
fact: «An old gravestone» in a churchyard can teach us about people from the past.
fact: «Departed this life» means died, and it is old-fashioned wording found on old gravestones.
fact: «She loved and was loved» is a gravestone message that says what lasts.
exercise: What is a gravestone? | A stone bench in a park | A tall church tower with a bell | A wall built around a field | *A stone put on a grave, with a name and words about the person
exercise: «Departed this life» is written on an old gravestone. What does it mean? | *Died | Moved house | Got married | Went on holiday
exercise: In a history lesson, what can pupils learn from «the words on the gravestone»? | How to swim fast | What the weather will be tomorrow | How to cook a meal | *Something about people from the past
test: Which phrase from the lesson means died? | "A good innings" | *"Departed this life" | "The words on the gravestone" | "An old gravestone"
test: A gravestone says «She loved and was loved». What does that say? | How much money was spent on the grave | What the weather was like that day | *What lasts | Which team won the match
exam: «A good innings» comes from cricket. What does it mean? | A broken window | *A long, full life | A ball thrown very far | A short game played in the rain
